**TestNG Annotations** control test execution flow and setup/teardown operations.

**Execution Order:**

```
@BeforeSuite       (Once before all tests in suite)
    |
    ├── @BeforeTest    (Before <test> tag in testng.xml)
    |       |
    |       ├── @BeforeClass  (Once before all methods in class)
    |       |       |
    |       |       ├── @BeforeMethod  (Before each test method)
    |       |       |       |
    |       |       |       └── @Test  (Actual test)
    |       |       |       |
    |       |       └── @AfterMethod   (After each test method)
    |       |       |
    |       └── @AfterClass   (Once after all methods in class)
    |       |
    └── @AfterTest     (After <test> tag)
    |
@AfterSuite        (Once after all tests in suite)
```

**Annotation Details:**

**@BeforeSuite**
```java
@BeforeSuite
public void beforeSuite() {
    // Setup database connections
    // Load global configuration
    // Initialize reporting
}
```
- Runs once before entire test suite
- Use for suite-level setup

**@BeforeClass**
```java
@BeforeClass
public void setUp() {
    // Initialize WebDriver
    driver = new ChromeDriver();
    driver.manage().window().maximize();
}
```
- Runs once before all test methods in class
- Perfect for browser initialization

**@BeforeMethod**
```java
@BeforeMethod
public void beforeEachTest() {
    // Navigate to starting page
    driver.get("https://example.com");
    // Clear cookies
}
```
- Runs before each @Test method
- Ensures clean state for each test

**@Test**
```java
@Test(priority = 1, groups = {"smoke"})
public void loginTest() {
    // Actual test code
}
```
- The actual test method
- Can have attributes (priority, groups, etc.)

**@AfterMethod**
```java
@AfterMethod
public void afterEachTest() {
    // Take screenshot if failed
    // Clear test data
}
```
- Runs after each @Test method
- Good for cleanup and reporting

**@AfterClass**
```java
@AfterClass
public void tearDown() {
    // Close browser
    if (driver != null) {
        driver.quit();
    }
}
```
- Runs once after all test methods
- Perfect for browser cleanup

**@AfterSuite**
```java
@AfterSuite
public void afterSuite() {
    // Close database connections
    // Generate final reports
}
```
- Runs once after entire suite
- Use for final cleanup

**Complete Example:**
```java
import org.testng.annotations.*;

public class AnnotationDemo {

    @BeforeSuite
    public void beforeSuite() {
        System.out.println("1. Before Suite");
    }

    @BeforeClass
    public void beforeClass() {
        System.out.println("2. Before Class");
    }

    @BeforeMethod
    public void beforeMethod() {
        System.out.println("3. Before Method");
    }

    @Test
    public void test1() {
        System.out.println("4. Test 1");
    }

    @Test
    public void test2() {
        System.out.println("4. Test 2");
    }

    @AfterMethod
    public void afterMethod() {
        System.out.println("5. After Method");
    }

    @AfterClass
    public void afterClass() {
        System.out.println("6. After Class");
    }

    @AfterSuite
    public void afterSuite() {
        System.out.println("7. After Suite");
    }
}
```

**Output:**
```
1. Before Suite
2. Before Class
3. Before Method
4. Test 1
5. After Method
3. Before Method
4. Test 2
5. After Method
6. After Class
7. After Suite
```

