**Common Selenium Mistakes and Solutions:**

**1. Not Using Waits**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
driver.get("https://example.com");
driver.findElement(By.id("username")).sendKeys("user");
// NoSuchElementException - element not loaded yet
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
driver.get("https://example.com");
WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));
WebElement username = wait.until(
    ExpectedConditions.visibilityOfElementLocated(By.id("username"))
);
username.sendKeys("user");
```

**2. Using Thread.sleep()**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
driver.findElement(By.id("submit")).click();
Thread.sleep(5000);  // Fixed wait, wastes time
driver.findElement(By.id("result")).getText();
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
driver.findElement(By.id("submit")).click();
WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));
WebElement result = wait.until(
    ExpectedConditions.visibilityOfElementLocated(By.id("result"))
);
result.getText();
```

**3. Not Closing Browser**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
public void testLogin() {
    WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();
    driver.get("https://example.com");
    // Test logic
    // Browser never closes - memory leak
}
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
public class LoginTest extends BaseTest {
    @AfterMethod(alwaysRun = true)
    public void tearDown() {
        if (driver != null) {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}
```

**4. Using Absolute XPath**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
// Breaks when HTML structure changes
driver.findElement(By.xpath(
    "/html/body/div[1]/div[2]/form/input[1]"
));
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
// Relative XPath - more maintainable
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//input[@id='username']"));

// Or better - use CSS
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("#username"));

// Best - use ID
driver.findElement(By.id("username"));
```

**5. Not Switching to Frames**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
// Element is in iframe, but not switching
driver.findElement(By.id("frameElement")).click();
// NoSuchElementException
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
// Switch to frame first
driver.switchTo().frame("frameName");
driver.findElement(By.id("frameElement")).click();
driver.switchTo().defaultContent();
```

**6. Not Maximizing Browser**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();
driver.get("https://example.com");
// Elements may be hidden in small window
driver.findElement(By.id("hiddenButton")).click();
// ElementNotInteractableException
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();
driver.manage().window().maximize();
driver.get("https://example.com");
```

**7. Mixing Implicit and Explicit Waits**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
driver.manage().timeouts().implicitlyWait(Duration.ofSeconds(10));
WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(20));
// Can cause unexpected timeouts (10 + 20 = 30 seconds)
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
// Use ONLY explicit waits
WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));
wait.until(ExpectedConditions.visibilityOfElementLocated(By.id("id")));
```

**8. Not Handling StaleElementException**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
WebElement element = driver.findElement(By.id("dynamic"));
driver.navigate().refresh();
element.click();  // StaleElementReferenceException
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
WebElement element = driver.findElement(By.id("dynamic"));
driver.navigate().refresh();
// Re-locate element after refresh
element = driver.findElement(By.id("dynamic"));
element.click();
```

**9. Hard-Coding Test Data**

❌ **Mistake:**
```java
@Test
public void testLogin() {
    driver.findElement(By.id("username")).sendKeys("hardcoded@test.com");
    driver.findElement(By.id("password")).sendKeys("hardcodedpass");
}
```

✅ **Solution:**
```java
