**Debugging Tips:**

1. **NoSuchElementException:**
   - Add explicit wait
   - Verify element exists (use browser DevTools)
   - Check if element is in frame
   - Ensure page is fully loaded

2. **ElementNotInteractableException:**
   - Maximize browser window
   - Scroll to element
   - Wait for element to be clickable
   - Check if element is covered by another element

3. **StaleElementReferenceException:**
   - Re-locate element after page changes
   - Use fresh locators instead of storing elements

4. **TimeoutException:**
   - Increase wait timeout
   - Verify expected condition is correct
   - Check if element appears at all

**Best Practice Summary:**
✅ Always use explicit waits
✅ Prefer ID/CSS over XPath
✅ Maximize browser in setup
✅ Close browser in teardown
✅ Switch to frames when needed
✅ Externalize test data
✅ Handle exceptions properly
✅ Use BaseTest pattern
✅ Implement Page Object Model
✅ Don't use Thread.sleep()

